# Rest Parameters (`...args: type[]`) 🧺

Type variable-length arguments using rest syntax with an array type:

```typescript
function computeAverage(category: string, ...scores: number[]): string {
  const total = scores.reduce((sum, s) => sum + s, 0);
  const avg = scores.length > 0 ? (total / scores.length).toFixed(1) : "0";
  return `${category} Average: ${avg}`;
}

console.log(computeAverage("Math", 90, 85, 95));
console.log(computeAverage("Physics", 78, 82, 88, 92));
```

