# Typing Callback Functions 📞

Functions that receive callbacks can enforce strict types on the callback arguments and return value:

```typescript
function executeWithRetry(
  task: () => boolean,
  onFailure: (attempt: number) => void
): boolean {
  for (let i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {
    if (task()) return true;
    onFailure(i);
  }
  return false;
}

executeWithRetry(
  () => false,
  (attempt) => console.log(`Attempt ${attempt} failed, retrying...`)
);
```

