# Object Types: `readonly` Properties 🔒

Mark properties as `readonly` to prevent reassignment after object initialization:

```typescript
type DatabaseConfig = {
  readonly host: string;
  readonly port: number;
  database: string; // Mutable
};

const config: DatabaseConfig = {
  host: "localhost",
  port: 5432,
  database: "prod_db"
};

// config.port = 8080; // Error: Cannot assign to 'port' because it is a read-only property!
config.database = "staging_db"; // Valid!

console.log("Config:", config);
```

