# Function Overloading 🔀

When a function can be called with different parameter counts or types that return different results, use **function overloads**:

```typescript
// Overload signatures (contract declarations)
function combine(a: number, b: number): number;
function combine(a: string, b: string): string;

// Implementation signature (handles all cases)
function combine(a: any, b: any): any {
  return a + b;
}

const numResult = combine(10, 20);     // Type is inferred as 'number'
const strResult = combine("A", "B");   // Type is inferred as 'string'

console.log("Combined numbers:", numResult);
console.log("Combined strings:", strResult);
```

