# Destructuring Typed Objects in Function Signatures 📐

Clean syntax for typed parameter destructuring:

```typescript
type UserOptions = {
  username: string;
  age?: number;
  role?: string;
};

function registerUser({ username, age = 18, role = "Member" }: UserOptions): string {
  return `Registered ${username}, Age ${age}, Role ${role}`;
}

console.log(registerUser({ username: "David" }));
console.log(registerUser({ username: "Elena", age: 30, role: "Admin" }));
```

