# Introduction to Generic Functions 🧬

Generics allow functions to work across a variety of types while retaining full type safety:

```typescript
// Type variable <T> captures the input type!
function identity<T>(arg: T): T {
  return arg;
}

const output1 = identity<string>("myString"); // Type is string
const output2 = identity<number>(100);          // Type is number

console.log("Output 1:", output1);
console.log("Output 2:", output2);
```

